      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "beat": 6
      },
      "text": "The most expensive mistake in business is treating a prototype like a product.\n\nA prototype is funded for LEARNING and judged on what you found out.\nA product is funded for REVENUE and judged on money. Swap them and you either\ncancel an experiment for missing a target it never had, or bet the company on\nsomething nobody tested. Both look, from the inside, exactly like being decisive.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The most expensive mistake in business is treating a prototype like a product.\n\nA prototype is funded for LEARNING and judged on what you found out.\nA product is funded for REVENUE and judged on money. Swap them and you either\ncancel an experiment for missing a target it never had, or bet the company on\nsomething nobody tested. Both look, from the inside, exactly like being decisive.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 14
    }
  ],
